<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I824be388cc3b094c889683f71485a8af6b760006" commit="5c719344aab5747dce5efc5fa199f47abfe95b13" commit_message="Make extract_param() not change the input buffer  extract_param() was introduced many years ago in upstream and has always removed the &quot;needle&quot; from the &quot;haystack&quot;.  The best reason for that approach is to detect if there are unused parameters specified which could be an indication that the user misspelled a parameter or some other silly mistake.  More importantly though, multiple programmers init functions should be able to parse the same parameters so that if init for one device fails, we can gracefully fall thru to try another which may use the same parameters. This is especially true for the ECs we support.  Long-term, the fix should be to parse the programmer parameters into a linked list so that we can detect unused parameters, detect duplicate parameters, and possibly other useful things. In the short- term though we need to make extract_param() non-destructive.  BUG=chromium:658207 BRANCH=none TEST=tested on reef with follow-up patch  Change-Id: I824be388cc3b094c889683f71485a8af6b760006 Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/402057 Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="402057" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/57/402057/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7d0d2969ce7ddd707cefae1f5c6c5d38c7c7b935" commit="d2c0c2fe52e0f791e9e78baecdf2ec361a02627c" commit_message="cros_ec_*: Err out if non-EC type parameter is used for LPC/I2C  CrOS ECs come in a few diffrent varieties now: EC, PD, and SH. The way things evolved over time we never really worried about what happens if the user specifies pd or sh as the EC type on a system with an LPC or I2C CrOS EC.  Consequently &quot;-p ec:type=&lt;sh|pd&gt;&quot; causes flashrom to get confused and act as though &quot;-p ec:type=ec&quot; was used if the EC is I2C or LPC. This probably doesn't matter for most cases (firmware read/write) since the sizes would mismatch or some other obvious failure would occur, but other commands could return information about the EC instead of the device the user intends to target.  BUG=chromium:658207 BRANCH=none TEST=tested on reef, &quot;flashrom -p ec:type=&quot; fails when pd or sh are specified.  Change-Id: I7d0d2969ce7ddd707cefae1f5c6c5d38c7c7b935 Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/402058 Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="402058" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/58/402058/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3f055d320c89cecc927f7ac3e2898883330a6f76" commit="a9cc4b52f0a854dfe4d9eb4c61f4f0e2bcfc644f" commit_message="sys-devel/gcc: set the default sysroot for clang in the sysroot wrapper.  Default sysroot for gcc is set during configure.  BUG=chromium:655320 TEST=Running armv7a-cros-linux-gnueabi-clang without SYSROOT environment variable picks the right default sysroot.  Change-Id: I3f055d320c89cecc927f7ac3e2898883330a6f76 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/399399 Commit-Ready: Rahul Chaudhry &lt;rahulchaudhry@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Rahul Chaudhry &lt;rahulchaudhry@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Rahul Chaudhry &lt;rahulchaudhry@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="399399" owner_email="rahulchaudhry@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/99/399399/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3c4442925b321c298e7e81fc20b93cd8eb025846" commit="a27dfbae2cbcf39216a939f6c04747c2cbc113af" commit_message="Change hotrod suite to run on all channels and add job retry  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I3c4442925b321c298e7e81fc20b93cd8eb025846 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/402229 Commit-Ready: Harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="402229" owner_email="harpreet@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/29/402229/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3dd72e398b8276ccb3c71340ce5eccb4048c1034" commit="b7aa5f7d8001c9983f4f6935b571b172e9560e36" commit_message="Move buildbucket_build_status constants to lib/constants.py  To track slave builds using buildbucket, we will collect and process build statuses in different places. lib/constants.py is a better place to hold the buidlbucket_build_status (like the build statuses from CIDB).  BUG=chromium:655295 TEST=unit_tests  Change-Id: I3dd72e398b8276ccb3c71340ce5eccb4048c1034 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/399701 Commit-Ready: Ningning Xia &lt;nxia@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ningning Xia &lt;nxia@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="399701" owner_email="nxia@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/01/399701/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8e8feb788bd8dfca0b53581d4ffe3cb79e57ea32" commit="b1b4af743e5f7db7d1c2d2807803a41d36da942f" commit_message="permission_broker:  Add missing header &lt;sys/stat.h&gt; to usb_driver_tracker.cc  usb_driver_tracker.cc needs the definition for 'struct stat' from this header.  Currently, it relies on getting it included indirectly through &lt;libudev.h&gt;.  Make the dependency explicit here, to prevent any future breakage when the package owning &lt;libudev.h&gt; is upgraded or if systemd is used.  BUG=chromium:583671 TEST=Built the package.  Change-Id: I8e8feb788bd8dfca0b53581d4ffe3cb79e57ea32 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/400765 Commit-Ready: Sabin Floares &lt;sabin.floares@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Sabin Floares &lt;sabin.floares@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="400765" owner_email="sabin.floares@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/65/400765/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic5ef86eaf9c9b0d38fe5e6d55f9d1721a45f246b" commit="1f41fc2ac8b0fa1c0eb916e8e49d5aca2ad366f7" commit_message="container_utils: refactor device_jail use of permission_broker  In order to make this more testable in the future we should abstract out the permission broker client functionality, so that DeviceJails can be used with mock permission brokers for testing.  Since this is expanding past one file I also felt it was time to split this out into its own subdirectory.  BUG=None TEST=check that functionality has not changed on a DUT  Change-Id: Ic5ef86eaf9c9b0d38fe5e6d55f9d1721a45f246b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/401650 Commit-Ready: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chirantan Ekbote &lt;chirantan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="401650" owner_email="ejcaruso@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/50/401650/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="8930.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>